  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ac90323-d753-42e2-8ead-ce3bf65fe1bc"],
 " returns."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"09f1125f-cc11-4e29-abc6-91cca93264ae"],

Cell["\<\
Two conditions, and the asymmetry between them is the whole definition:\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a35482dc-deec-4c9c-bfe9-3de9d320782e"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4a542e80-7e33-4395-b99b-23d23b9cd20c"], Cell["Condition", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"0f496bf7-374d-4f2b-bdf4-5c78e9282c1d"],
     Cell["Why", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"8f208d4d-c0c9-488c-8a96-039e0269e1c8"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "1a771047-be6c-4b53-889c-959f90abe91b"], Cell[
    "the sequence is a shortest path", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "548c4775-3f86-46ec-a63b-a8760861a4fe"], Cell[TextData[{
     "a ray is straight, so ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      TemplateBox[{
        Cell[
         TextData["InfraSegmentQ"]], 
        "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegmentQ", 
        "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
       "PackageLink",
       BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "0514f053-ce6d-44e9-8e51-fab25102a8e0"],
     " must hold"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8e064694-1ce8-4a18-af72-e33d32f560a1"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2d8f8ce9-77ff-4883-8ffd-87730a2e8039"], Cell["\<\
no neighbour of the last vertex sits one step farther from the first\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2da37180-0132-4fbc-a2cf-3820298cbbe3"], 
    Cell["the far end is inextensible", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "55be8229-b403-46b2-a14c-ce21193f3a9c"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"c773a9db-7bca-4ba2-aa8d-\
23dfd252806c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inextensibility is required ",
 StyleBox["only at the far end",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The origin is an endpoint by fiat \[LongDash] that is exactly what \
distinguishes a ray from a line (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraInfiniteLineQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraInfiniteLineQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "35aedb02-fd09-41d7-b585-0c75b32eb764"],
 " asks for inextensibility at both ends), and it means a ray may start \
anywhere, not only at a peripheral vertex."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aa810e77-f487-4a75-8dd9-a660ade279a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sequences shorter than two vertices are ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0152efa2-b7b1-4882-bd4d-b6b4e2f2cd58"],
 ": a single vertex has no direction."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3d502e77-dea2-48c4-a7b2-e010c860f360"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The predicate is the companion of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraHalfLine"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraHalfLine", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1f62894f-9d7d-407d-8487-83e6a8033c72"],
 ", which prolongs a shortest path outward until no neighbour prolongs it, so \
every ray that finder returns satisfies it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"12f13849-dfdd-402b-b64e-d86a75f675ec"]
}, Open  ]],

